---
layout: layouts/base.njk
title: "The Defender Family — Overlanding & Documentary Storytelling"
description: "Family-led storytelling studio producing cinematic travel, documentary, and impact stories for destinations, hospitality brands, and NGOs. 25+ years of editorial photography on the road."
ogImage: "/images/uploads/the-defender-family-open-graph.jpg"
ogImageAlt: "The Defender Family with their Land Rover Defender on a remote road"
priority: "1.0"
lang: "en"
translations:
  - { lang: "es", url: "/es/" }
defaultUrl: "/"
---

<!-- HERO -->
<section class="hero">
  <div class="hero-bg hero-bg--video">
    <video id="hero-video" autoplay muted loop playsinline preload="auto"></video>
    <script>
      (function(){
        var v = document.getElementById('hero-video');
        var src = window.innerWidth <= 768
          ? '/images/uploads/hero-mobile.mp4'
          : '/images/uploads/hero-desktop.mp4';
        var s = document.createElement('source');
        s.src = src; s.type = 'video/mp4';
        v.appendChild(s);
        v.load();
      })();
    </script>
  </div>
  <div class="hero-content" style="text-align: center; display: flex; flex-direction: column; align-items: center;">
    <h1>Remarkable places<br class="mobile-br"> <em>Real stories</em></h1>
    <p class="hero-sub" style="text-align: center;">Family overlanding. Documentary photography. Immersive 360.</p>
    <a href="/work-with-us/" class="btn">Work with us</a>
  </div>
</section>

<!-- INTRO -->
<section class="intro">
  <div class="container">
    <div class="intro-inner fade-up">
      <div class="intro-text">
        <h2>A family trip, then another, then something clicked</h2>
        <p>TDF began the way most good things do: organically, as something we were already doing. A family that travels, documents, and tells stories. Rafa with his cameras and creativity. Mariella building projects with impact. Sophie growing up and discovering the world on the road.</p>
        <p>Over time, we realised those pieces fit together naturally: the real places we reached, the stories we found along the way, and the 360/VR content we captured could have a second life through Reality Telling, our social impact company working in hospitals and care homes. Travelling, building access, producing cinematic content, and bringing immersive experiences to people who cannot physically reach those places stopped being a coincidence and started becoming a model.</p>
        <p>That is what this is about now: real access, real presence, and cinematic content with a life beyond the journey, in media, brands, institutions, and also in a hospital room.<p>
        <a href="/projects/" class="btn btn-dark">See how we work</a>
      </div>
      <div class="intro-image">
        {% image "/images/uploads/the-defender-family-posing-scotland.jpg", "The Defender Family on the road" %}
      </div>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>

<!-- PILLARS -->
<section class="pillars">
  <div class="container">
    <div class="section-label">What we do</div>
    <h2 class="section-heading">Three ways we tell the story</h2>
    <div class="pillars-grid">
      <a class="pillar fade-up" href="/stories/">
        {% image "/images/uploads/the-defender-family-albania-river.jpg", "Family travel storytelling", "lazy", "(max-width: 768px) 100vw, 33vw", "pillar-img" %}
        <div class="pillar-num">01 — Travel Family</div>
        <h3>Travel and Destination Storytelling</h3>
        <p>For tourism boards, national parks, and hospitality brands that need travel content with real texture. We embed properly, stay long enough to find the story, and deliver cinematic photo and video that feels lived-in because it is.</p>
      </a>
      <a class="pillar fade-up" href="/rafa-lanus/">
        {% image "/images/uploads/bolivian-man-by-rafa-lanus.jpg", "Impact documentary storytelling", "lazy", "(max-width: 768px) 100vw, 33vw", "pillar-img" %}
        <div class="pillar-num">02 — Photography</div>
        <h3>Editorial and Documentary Photography</h3>
        <p>For publishers, cultural institutions, and NGOs that need field photography with depth and institutional sensitivity. From portraiture to documentary sequences, available for commission and editorial licensing.</p>
      </a>
      <a class="pillar fade-up" href="/projects/">
        {% image "/images/uploads/woman-swimming-underwater.jpg", "Editorial photography", "lazy", "(max-width: 768px) 100vw, 33vw", "pillar-img" %}
        <div class="pillar-num">03 — Impact stories</div>
        <h3>Immersive 360/VR experiences</h3>
        <p>For destinations and healthcare partners that want to place people inside an experience. Produced through Reality Telling, our social company, built for clinical use, cultural programmes, and public engagement. Check <span style="color: var(--color-warm-dark); text-decoration: underline;">Reality Telling</span></p>
      </a>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>

<!-- FEATURED STORIES -->
<section class="stories">
  <div class="container">
    <div class="section-label">From the field</div>
    <h2 class="section-heading">Featured stories</h2>
    <p class="stories-sub">A selection of journeys, documentary moments, and field stories that reflect how we work.</p>
    <div class="stories-grid">
      {% for post in collections.stories | limit(6) %}
      <a class="story-card" href="{{ post.url }}">
        {% if post.data.heroImage %}{% image post.data.heroImage, (post.data.heroImageAlt or post.data.title), "lazy", "(max-width: 768px) 100vw, 33vw" %}{% endif %}
        <div class="story-info">
          <span>{{ post.data.category }}</span>
          <h3>{{ post.data.title }}</h3>
        </div>
      </a>
      {% endfor %}
    </div>
  </div>
</section>

<!-- WHY -->
<section class="side-section">
  <div class="container">
    <div class="side-inner fade-up">
      <div class="side-image">
        {% image "/images/uploads/girl-ice-skating-lake.jpg", "The family" %}
      </div>
      <div class="side-text">
        <h2>Not every story can be told from a desk</h2>
        <p>We're a field production studio that travels as a family. When we're somewhere remarkable, a cultural institution, a national park, a working community, we produce cinematic travel stories, documentary photography, and immersive 360/VR experiences simultaneously.</p>
        <p>One operation. Three outputs. For destinations, brands, and institutions that need more than a standard shoot.</p>
        <a href="/about/" class="btn btn-dark">More about us</a>
      </div>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>

<!-- CTA -->
<section class="cta-band">
  <div class="container">
    <h2>Let's build something<br>worth remembering</h2>
    <p>If you have a place worth documenting, a story that deserves more than standard coverage, or an institution that's never been filmed properly, reach out. That's usually where the best work starts.</p>
    <a href="/contact/" class="btn btn-dark">Start a collaboration</a>
  </div>
</section>
